# NATS Server 2.14.6 environment schema (@env-spec / varlock format).
#
# The compose pins nats:2.14-alpine. On 2026-08-29 (research date) that tag
# is byte-identical (same push timestamp) to nats:2.14.6-alpine, the newest
# patch on the 2.14 line.
#
# Source: grep of os.Getenv / os.LookupEnv across server/ in the
# nats-io/nats-server v2.14.6 tarball, plus the image's
# docker-entrypoint.sh and Dockerfile (nats-io/nats-docker, 2.14.x/alpine3.22
# at the matching commit). The server itself reads no environment beyond a
# couple of Windows-service-only lookups (NATS_DOCKERIZED, NATS_STARTUP_DELAY
# in server/service_windows.go, dead code on this Linux image) and $VAR
# substitution inside a `-c`/`--config` file (conf/parse.go), a feature this
# template does not use, since its compose passes --jetstream, --store_dir
# and --http_port directly on the command line with no config file. The
# image's entrypoint script reads no environment either: it only inspects
# argv to decide whether to prepend "nats-server" before exec'ing.
#
# Everything the server does (clustering, auth, TLS, leafnodes, JetStream
# limits) is a config-file directive or a command-line flag, not an
# environment variable. This template runs unauthenticated, TLS-terminated-
# at-the-edge, single-node JetStream; see @docs for the flag/config list.

# @defaultSensitive=false @defaultRequired=infer
# @docs("NATS Docker image guide", https://docs.nats.io/running-a-nats-service/nats_admin/nats_docker)
# ---

# ─── Core ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing here is required. Configuration is command-line flags (this
# compose) or a mounted config file, never the environment.

# IANA timezone name (e.g. America/New_York). nats-server timestamps log
# lines with the local timezone by default (logtime_utc defaults to false),
# via Go's time.Now(), which honors TZ the same way any process on Linux
# does. Empty defaults to the image's built-in UTC.
# @docs("NATS logging configuration", https://docs.nats.io/running-a-nats-service/configuration/logging)
TZ=
